WEBVTT

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:06.060
East Hand 1

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:06.060
Dealer - 
Takakamo Shizuno

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.530
<i>It looks like Oohoshi-san's going 
to have another double riichi.</i>

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:13.530
<i>In order to stop that...</i>

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.530
<i>Someone needs to get a chi or pon first!</i>

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:19.490
<i>This?</i>

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.090
<i>No good...</i>

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:29.670
<i>Nobody could call it.</i>

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.010
<i>Then Oohoshi's...</i>

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:36.260
Riichi!

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:39.300
<i>Straight discard into a double riichi?!</i>

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.260
<i>She was in tenpai from the get-go.</i>

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:43.570
<i>Which means she was only one 
tile away from a chihou?!</i>

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:43.570
[Chihou - winning with your first draw, yakuman hand]

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:52.940
<b>The Path</b>

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:53.150
Kan.

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:55.860
<i>Here it is.</i>

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:17.130
Ron.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:21.850
Double riichi, four ura dora.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:24.730
12,000.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.980
<i>Yet another kan from one of the ura dora!</i>

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:31.180
<i>Another double riichi with a 
kan leading to four ura dora.</i>

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:33.480
<i>Is this Oohoshi Awai's power?</i>

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:36.330
<i>So, I can still win.</i>

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:39.290
<i>I was just a little out of focus earlier.</i>

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:43.740
So double riichi is Oohoshi 
Awai's attack style?

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:46.240
Don't forget the ura dora from the kan.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:48.230
In the West Tokyo preliminaries,

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:49.820
her winning hands had them, too.

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:52.380
Without those, it would 
just be a double riichi.

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:56.580
Which means that it's safe 
until she declares a kan.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:59.240
Ippatsu are basically accidents, 
so we should just

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:01.760
pressure her heavily and crush her first.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:04.750
I think that's a sound strategy,

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:06.100
but everybody except Oohoshi has

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.000
a starting hand at least five tiles from tenpai.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:10.790
We're stuck here...

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:14.270
But Oohoshi wasn't able to 
win the last hand of the first half.

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:15.590
That's it.

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:17.580
I wonder what was different then.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:18.900
Hey,

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:22.050
did you tell Ryuuka what 
you figured out so far?

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:24.660
Yes, briefly during the break.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:29.670
Okay, then let's keep researching 
and leave today to Ryuuka.

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:32.790
East Hand 2

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:32.790
Dealer - 
Shimizudani Ryuuka

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:33.370
<i>I'm dealer, so I want to call on Toki,</i>

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:37.130
<i>but Shirouzu Mairu won this hand 
in the fourth players' match,</i>

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:39.800
<i>so Tsuruta Himeko might win.</i>

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:44.300
<i>In that case, I'll play like I always do: 
with my own power, at full strength!</i>

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:50.310
<i>This hand, too?</i>

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:53.940
Riichi.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:59.220
<i>So you don't care that our captain</i>

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:00.450
<i>won this hand, Oohoshi.</i>

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:03.700
<i>I haven't tried double riichi 
against you guys yet...</i>

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:06.160
<i>Mind if I give it a shot?</i>

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:11.330
<i>This hand, our captain won with three 
han and the reservation was two...</i>

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:15.340
<i>I'll get a mangan!</i>

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:25.050
Ron. 8,000.

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:32.060
<i>Amazing, Shindouji! Seriously!</i>

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:34.060
That's surprising.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:36.050
So there are high school players besides

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:37.980
Teru who could beat Awai's double riichi.

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:40.700
I think there should be about 10.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:44.360
I think the Shindouji combo 
will be even more viable,

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:46.390
even at the pro level.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.290
I've beaten Oohoshi's 
double riichi before.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:53.270
Really? Awai-chan's?

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:55.420
Yeah... And I see you don't believe me...

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:56.880
How did you do it?

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:01.380
Well, after the dice were cast
and the dead wall was split off,

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:03.540
I connected the walls in a circular shape.

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:04.200
Hehehe

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:06.050
That's evil.

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:09.360
She was sobbing because she couldn't win.

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:14.120
Speaking of which, I wonder why she
 didn't win the last hand before.

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:16.860
Didn't Awai-chan do that on purpose?

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:21.020
East Hand 3

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:20.680
I feel like she was playing seriously.

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:23.190
Riichi.

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:26.810
<i>Oohoshi-san is dealer,</i>

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:29.510
<i>so calling to prevent double 
riichi isn't even an option.</i>

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:32.960
<i>This hand, our captain won 
without putting in a reservation,</i>

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.920
<i>so obviously there's no key.</i>

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:37.700
<i>I'll have to do my best on my own!</i>

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:42.460
<i>Himeko, don't push yourself too much. 
She's dealer right now.</i>

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:45.990
Kan.

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:48.430
<i>Here it is!</i>

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:50.470
<i>Oohoshi declared a kan again.</i>

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:53.180
<i>Oh well, I can't back down 
after I've come this far!</i>

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:55.560
<i>I'll push ahead!</i>

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:57.940
<i>It went through!</i>

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:07.820
<i>This is dangerous...</i>

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:10.160
Ron.

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:17.750
<i>Hm, I guess their combo wasn't active.</i>

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.500
18,000.

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:23.380
<i>As expected, ura dora from the kan.</i>

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:26.010
<i>Another double riichi with four dora!</i>

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:28.150
Bonus hand 1.

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:29.640
<i>Did you know?</i>

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:34.140
<i>As long as I stay dealer, my 
double riichi can't be stopped,</i>

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:37.390
<i>and Shindouji's weird combo 
won't be making an appearance.</i>

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:39.360
I get it. It's the corners.

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:40.420
Corners?

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:42.200
Oh, of the tile wall.

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:43.060
Exactly.

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:47.130
The wall of tiles that is 
created initially in mahjong,

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:51.700
Wall

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:51.700
Corner

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:49.880
also called the tile wall, has corners.

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:51.880
So the corner of the wall?

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:55.770
Oohoshi Awai declares her kan
right before the last corner,

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:58.260
and then wins right after that corner.

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:01.370
Well spotted.

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:03.320
It's not easy to figure 
that out from just the

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:05.000
usual video and play records.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:08.050
The dice rolls were recorded 
too, so I counted.

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:10.550
Did you tell Ryuuka about this?

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:12.890
No, I just realized it.

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:16.060
Oohoshi only won one hand 
with double riichi in the first half.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:20.020
The thing in common to the West 
Tokyo preliminaries double riichi

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:21.960
that I instantly realized then was that,

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:23.690
both times, a double riichi only hand

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:26.450
got a kan from one of the ura dora, 
and won right after the kan.

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:27.950
But that last hand of the first half...

00:06:28.290 --> 00:06:31.660
Oh, the hand Oohoshi didn't win?

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:35.150
But I couldn't figure out why that 
hand didn't go the same way,

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:38.410
so I couldn't say that she'd 
win right after her kan.

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:41.460
Right now, I regret only telling 
Ryuuka that she should

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:44.380
watch out after the kan.

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:48.420
Ron. 18,300.

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:53.180
<i>She called how many points before 
looking at the ura dora for the kan?!</i>

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:55.100
Now,

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:58.100
bonus hand 2!

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:00.850
<i>I won't let you stay dealer any longer!</i>

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:04.770
<i>I wanted to save these for later...</i>

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:06.380
<i>Toki!</i>

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:22.360
<i>I can see it!</i>

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:23.920
<i>That's a big one.</i>

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:26.990
<i>T-Toki...</i>

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:32.070
One more, at most.

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:33.260
Of what?

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:35.240
If I hadn't been hospitalized,

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:38.020
I could have stored more 
in Ryuuka's thighs.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:40.110
What are you talking about?

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:41.390
Sorry, Ryuuka...

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:44.400
for not being able to 
lie on your lap more.

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:45.770
Sensei!!

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:45.770
That's what you're sorry for?!

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:50.190
Ron.

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:52.930
16,600.

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:58.120
Aren't you going to check the ura dora?

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:01.120
I will, but I don't think it'll change.

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:07.140
<i>It's not just Shindouji!</i>

00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:13.520
<i>Shizu, can you make it over those 
three girls... those three mountains?</i>

00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:17.640
<i>Have you managed to push 
your way into their depths?</i>

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:22.270
<i>Nodoka said once in an interview</i>

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:26.030
<i>that she played by herself online 
for about a year and a half.</i>

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:29.120
<i>The time Nodoka spent alone wasn't wasted.</i>

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:31.230
<i>It helped shape who she is now.</i>

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:36.280
<i>All I did was run around the mountains 
by myself for two and a half years.</i>

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:41.530
<i>Compared to Nodoka, 
I was depressed at first,</i>

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:44.960
<i>but now it's different.</i>

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:49.430
<i>Because that's all giving me strength now!</i>

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:55.230
<i>The view is great!</i>

00:08:56.710 --> 00:08:59.390
You know the paths that mountain 
ascetics walk for their training?

00:08:59.860 --> 00:09:01.550
She ran around those, not to train,

00:09:01.550 --> 00:09:03.860
but as if they were her backyard.

00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:06.020
A girl... in the mountains?

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:10.850
I wonder what Shizuno found 
in those secluded places.

00:09:12.370 --> 00:09:14.700
Shizu always liked the mountains, huh?

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:16.800
She suddenly starts running,

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:20.120
and never gets lost there, even though 
her sense of direction is terrible.

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:22.910
Even when we taught her about mahjong...

00:09:23.630 --> 00:09:24.540
Mountain?

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:26.500
These walls are also called mountains?!

00:09:26.990 --> 00:09:28.280
That's right.

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:30.780
Which means that the mountains

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:33.430
I'll be running around will 
be different every time?!

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:34.270
Yes.

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:36.030
You're getting way too excited.

00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:40.030
Yeah, that did happen, huh?

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:41.190
Yeah.

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:43.770
Yuu, what do the dice say?

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:46.850
Um... Right 10.

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:51.310
10, huh? Then this hand might work, too.

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:52.980
East Hand 4

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:55.610
Ron.

00:09:57.410 --> 00:09:58.490
2,600.

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:02.030
<i>Achiga?!</i>

00:10:02.650 --> 00:10:04.160
<i>That cheap hand?!</i>

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:08.920
Could this be?

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:11.750
Here comes a Hiroko epiphany.

00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:15.860
It's just a guess, but I think
 Oohoshi Awai switched to her

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:18.410
attack mode in the last 
hand of the first half.

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:19.550
With that double riichi?

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:22.860
Since then, she declared 
double riichi every hand

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:25.500
and everybody's starting 
hands were quite slow.

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:28.190
Normally there'd be no 
way to win against that,

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:33.020
but the Shindouji combo 
completely defeated that.

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:35.440
It seems that their starting 
hands were not affected, either.

00:10:35.770 --> 00:10:38.610
They say even pros can't handle that combo.

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:41.350
It's more or less certain that
there will be a counted yakuman

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:43.080
in South Hand 3 for them.

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:45.350
That doesn't sound good.

00:10:45.350 --> 00:10:48.940
There were three hands where Oohashi 
declared a double riichi that

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:51.490
she didn't win, excluding the ones 
with the Shindouji combo.

00:10:51.490 --> 00:10:54.290
One of them was 
Shimizudani-senpai's baiman.

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:57.030
She glided into tenpai and straight to a win.

00:10:57.680 --> 00:10:59.140
There's something there.

00:10:59.140 --> 00:11:01.310
The problems are the other two.

00:11:01.310 --> 00:11:05.480
Yeah, in both, that 
first-year from Achiga won.

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:06.310
Exactly!

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:09.380
What I just noticed is the eyes of the dice.

00:11:09.380 --> 00:11:10.620
What do you mean?

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:12.980
Oohoshi wins her double riichi hands

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:14.560
with the last wall.

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:17.470
The dice decide where the corner will be.

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:20.540
I finally get it.

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:21.480
Yes.

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:23.390
When Oohoshi won her double riichi hands,

00:11:23.390 --> 00:11:25.410
the dice showed 3 to 7.

00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:28.990
Conversely, when Takakamo won,
 they showed 2 or 10.

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:34.160
The corners were deep in the wall!

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:38.710
I was about to say that...

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:43.310
In the last hand of the first half,
 the dice showed 2.

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:45.760
That doesn't seem that deep,

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:47.980
but I guess it was deeper 
than the other hands.

00:11:47.980 --> 00:11:50.310
Oohoshi was able to make her kan,

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:52.060
so I guess her territory begins there.

00:11:52.430 --> 00:11:54.810
Territory? Whose?

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:56.540
That would be...

00:11:57.510 --> 00:11:59.460
the master of the deep mountains.

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:02.280
South Hand 1

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:03.780
<i>Come to think of it,</i>

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:05.850
<i>ever since around the South 
round of the first half...</i>

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:10.390
<i>As those hands went on, and 
we got deeper into the wall,</i>

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:13.330
<i>the worse my field of vision 
got, as if there was a haze.</i>

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:17.590
<i>Moreover, there's something there...</i>

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:19.510
<i>Ah, jeez!</i>

00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:23.470
<i>I will not lose to something so nondescript!</i>

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:25.090
Riichi!

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:26.850
<i>A double riichi again!</i>

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:30.810
<i>The last corner is really deep...</i>

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:32.370
It looks like this hand

00:12:32.370 --> 00:12:35.960
will be concluded deep in the 
wall "mountain," but I wonder...

00:12:38.350 --> 00:12:39.330
<i>Back then,</i>

00:12:40.620 --> 00:12:43.300
<i>I was alone in the mountains a lot.</i>

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:46.620
<i>I feel like, because of that,</i>

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:49.170
<i>I was able to get a clear sense of who I am</i>

00:12:49.170 --> 00:12:51.700
<i>and had a lot of time to think.</i>

00:12:52.970 --> 00:12:56.000
<i>At some point, my 
consciousness melted into nature,</i>

00:12:56.000 --> 00:13:01.090
<i>and I felt like I had become one 
with all of the deep mountains.</i>

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:05.970
<i>Right now, the wall "mountain" 
and my opponents</i>

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:07.930
<i>feel like the mountains from back then!</i>

00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:10.430
<i>Now the kan...</i>

00:13:13.260 --> 00:13:17.020
<i>I can't?! Again? Why?!</i>

00:13:17.800 --> 00:13:18.650
I see.

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:22.450
Koromo-chan's haitei and my rinshan tiles

00:13:22.450 --> 00:13:24.360
are also deep in the wall.

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:25.780
Don't use "chan" with me.

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:30.090
<i>So depending on the dice roll, 
the fifth player for my sister's team...</i>

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:32.290
<i>So it is her...</i>

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:49.180
Ron.

00:13:51.380 --> 00:13:52.810
11,600.

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:55.310
<i>Achiga Girls' strikes again!</i>

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:57.690
<i>A hit on Shiraitodai!</i>

00:13:57.690 --> 00:14:01.190
<i>For the first time, 
Achiga Girls' is in first place!</i>

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:03.750
It is the first time, right?

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:06.370
<i>You weren't sure?!</i>

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:07.330
Achiga...

00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:09.860
Beyond the mountain path for training,

00:14:09.860 --> 00:14:12.980
beyond the recesses of perpetual change,

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:15.210
the incarnation of the deepest

00:14:15.210 --> 00:14:17.210
ravines of the mountains, Shizuno, awaits.

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:19.490
Can the flower bloom against her on that ridge?

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:27.920
South Hand 1, Bonus 1

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:27.920
Dealer - Takakamo Shizuno

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:28.620
<i>Achiga... So she can disable</i>

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:31.350
<i>people's powers if it's deep in the wall?</i>

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:34.010
<i>However, since I control the openings,</i>

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:35.760
<i>the deep areas of the 
wall can only be built</i>

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:37.170
<i>with the remaining tiles.</i>

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:39.730
<i>That means she doesn't 
control everything.</i>

00:14:46.680 --> 00:14:48.100
<i>No double riichi?</i>

00:14:50.020 --> 00:14:53.350
<i>My starting hand isn't 
 five tiles from tenpai anymore.</i>

00:14:53.350 --> 00:14:54.160
<i>This is...</i>

00:14:57.490 --> 00:14:58.590
Riichi.

00:14:58.590 --> 00:14:59.630
<i>Is it the opposite?</i>

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:02.810
<i>Did Achiga's control over the deep areas</i>

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:05.090
<i>influence the opening turns, too?</i>

00:15:05.570 --> 00:15:08.630
<i>This didn't happen even when 
Teru took me in back then.</i>

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:10.090
<i>What is this?!</i>

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:15.560
<i>Is Oohoshi Awai's control waning?</i>

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:17.560
<i>Then I should...</i>

00:15:22.370 --> 00:15:23.500
<i>Body temperature.</i>

00:15:24.210 --> 00:15:25.180
<i>Heart rate.</i>

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:27.190
<i>Breathing.</i>

00:15:28.460 --> 00:15:30.280
<i>...heighten my five senses to the max.</i>

00:15:35.800 --> 00:15:37.640
<i>Looks like tenpai to my left.</i>

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:44.460
That's...

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:47.170
<i>Don't overdo it, Ryuuka.</i>

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:48.920
She's in the zone.

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:51.270
Yes, we should be good now.

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:53.550
Kan.

00:16:01.050 --> 00:16:03.480
Ron. 4,200.

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:10.110
<i>She got rid of the south pair to wait to 
triple up one of the non-yaku winds?</i>

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:13.640
<i>She hoarded my winning tiles!</i>

00:16:14.510 --> 00:16:16.080
<i>I'm finally dealer!</i>

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:18.930
<i>The last time!</i>

00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:21.400
<i>Toki!</i>

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:24.860
<i>What?!</i>

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:31.950
<i>If she can't see the path,</i>

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:34.500
<i>that means it'll be a draw, 
or someone else will win.</i>

00:16:34.920 --> 00:16:38.850
<i>However, already knowing that is helpful.</i>

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:38.850
South Hand 2

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:38.850
Turn 6

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:51.030
<i>She ignored it?!</i>

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:54.240
Tsumo. 300, 500.

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:57.990
<i>She ignored the 1,300 win to 
go for a trash tsumo win?</i>

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:00.490
<i>What was that win?!</i>

00:17:00.780 --> 00:17:02.030
That girl...

00:17:02.030 --> 00:17:05.170
Shizu sometimes plays 
completely instinctively.

00:17:06.160 --> 00:17:08.750
It almost always looks like a 
mistake at first glance, but...

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:11.510
She can see something, right?

00:17:11.900 --> 00:17:12.880
Yes.

00:17:13.350 --> 00:17:16.010
<i>Only two hands left in this semifinal!</i>

00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:18.760
The second to last hand: South Hand 3!

00:17:25.870 --> 00:17:27.830
<i>South Hand 3 of the second half.</i>

00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:32.050
<i>Shirouzu Mairu won a baiman 
hand in the previous match.</i>

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:36.280
<i>I don't want to give it up, but I 
don't want to deal into that, either.</i>

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:39.280
<i>It could be anything from a 
 sanbaiman to a counted yakuman.</i>

00:17:44.390 --> 00:17:46.910
<i>You can have a yakuman,</i>

00:17:46.910 --> 00:17:49.370
<i>but since I'm dealer,</i>

00:17:49.370 --> 00:17:51.380
<i>I have to stay on the offensive!</i>

00:17:52.150 --> 00:17:53.130
Riichi!

00:17:53.610 --> 00:17:54.630
<i>Knock yourself out.</i>

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:57.560
<i>But once again, I couldn't do a double riichi.</i>

00:17:58.610 --> 00:17:59.890
<i>What's going on?!</i>

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:02.740
<i>Huh? What is this?</i>

00:18:03.610 --> 00:18:06.200
<i>It's only natural that as your hand 
progresses, the number of tiles that</i>

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:07.770
<i>bring you closer to winning decreases,</i>

00:18:08.610 --> 00:18:11.480
<i>but when our combo was active, 
I didn't really feel that.</i>

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:14.700
<i>However, for a while now, as we 
keep going deeper into the "mountain,"</i>

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:16.020
<i>I can feel our captain less and less.</i>

00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:19.410
<i>This hasn't happened once 
since we formed our combo.</i>

00:18:20.390 --> 00:18:21.280
<i>Where are you?</i>

00:18:21.860 --> 00:18:22.930
<i>Himeko...</i>

00:18:35.770 --> 00:18:37.160
<i>Captain!</i>

00:18:40.230 --> 00:18:41.140
Tsumo!

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:43.170
8,000! 16,000!

00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:47.100
<i>A counted yakuman!</i>

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:48.990
<i>The dealer penalty...</i>

00:18:48.990 --> 00:18:51.270
<i>Is there really no way to stop this?</i>

00:18:51.710 --> 00:18:55.270
<i>I'm glad I was able to win, 
but it's still strange.</i>

00:18:55.270 --> 00:18:58.610
<i>Until now, the bond we have has 
never faltered, not even once.</i>

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:02.870
<i>Something deep in the 
"mountain" was interfering.</i>

00:19:03.440 --> 00:19:05.870
It's finally the last last hand!

00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:07.660
The point differential!

00:19:08.930 --> 00:19:11.630
The tile Achiga ignored in South 
Hand 2... it couldn't be...

00:19:12.850 --> 00:19:16.580
Awai shouldn't have declared 
riichi that hand.

00:19:19.810 --> 00:19:22.120
<i>This point differential!</i>

00:19:22.120 --> 00:19:23.480
<i>Even if I get</i>

00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:25.530
<i>a direct haneman hit off Achiga 
in first place, we will be tied.</i>

00:19:25.530 --> 00:19:27.530
<i>Because of dealer order precedence,</i>

00:19:27.530 --> 00:19:30.560
<i>Achiga will be in second place 
and we will be out in third!</i>

00:19:31.130 --> 00:19:35.480
<i>If Achiga had taken the 1,300 
point win instead last hand,</i>

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:38.400
<i>a direct haneman hit would 
have put us in second place.</i>

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:45.270
<i>I want to drag Achiga down from first 
place, but it's impossible now!</i>

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:47.910
South Hand 4

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:47.910
Last Hand

00:19:50.220 --> 00:19:51.490
<i>What is this?</i>

00:19:51.490 --> 00:19:53.670
<i>I can't even do a double 
riichi in the last hand!</i>

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:55.010
<i>This sucks!</i>

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:58.920
<i>The trash win after ignoring 
that tile in South Hand 2.</i>

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:02.160
<i>Does that mean she's only 
worried about Oohoshi?</i>

00:20:02.160 --> 00:20:04.540
<i>No, maybe she thinks that Shindouji</i>

00:20:04.540 --> 00:20:06.430
<i>and I won't be going for big hands?</i>

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:09.440
<i>Fact is, I can't call Toki any more,</i>

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:12.600
<i>so the best I can do is 
a cheap but fast win.</i>

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:15.110
<i>That'll be enough to make it to the finals</i>

00:20:15.110 --> 00:20:17.880
<i>and drop Shiraitodai out of the tournament.</i>

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:19.860
<i>I'll keep my defenses up</i>

00:20:20.750 --> 00:20:22.240
<i>and strike quickly with calling!</i>

00:20:22.770 --> 00:20:24.120
<i>I'm the last dealer.</i>

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:26.260
<i>Since I'm the dealer, with the dealer's streak,</i>

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:28.420
<i>I don't need to settle this with one strike.</i>

00:20:28.810 --> 00:20:30.500
<i>Luckily, I also have two dora,</i>

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:33.770
<i>so I'm going to win either way</i>

00:20:33.770 --> 00:20:35.000
<i>and make it to the finals!</i>

00:21:03.420 --> 00:21:06.940
<i>Yay, I got it! If I draw 
the last one, I'm second.</i>

00:21:06.940 --> 00:21:09.390
<i>Wait, I'm going for second place?</i>

00:21:10.520 --> 00:21:11.830
<i>This is humiliating!</i>

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:14.330
<i>Should I declare riichi?</i>

00:21:14.910 --> 00:21:18.010
<i>I need to draw it myself 
anyway, but with the riichi,</i>

00:21:18.010 --> 00:21:20.420
<i>I could get an ippatsu or win off Senriyama.</i>

00:21:22.700 --> 00:21:24.090
<i>Oh, I missed my chance.</i>

00:21:24.090 --> 00:21:24.880
Chi.

00:21:27.120 --> 00:21:29.760
<i>All right, I'm in tenpai.
 If I win, we're in the finals!</i>

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:32.450
<i>Just as I thought.</i>

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:34.680
<i>Even in the relative safety of first place,</i>

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:36.400
<i>you never know what might happen.</i>

00:21:36.910 --> 00:21:40.350
<i>Mahjong, the weather in the 
mountains, and the autumn sky!</i>

00:21:40.350 --> 00:21:41.490
<i>Even though it's summer.</i>

00:21:41.490 --> 00:21:42.360
Chi.

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:46.700
<i>Still one from tenpai...</i>

00:21:47.260 --> 00:21:49.240
<i>These girls are on the offensive.</i>

00:21:50.810 --> 00:21:51.540
<i>This!</i>

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:52.240
Kan!

00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:54.290
<i>I can still go for it!</i>

00:21:55.310 --> 00:21:56.210
Riichi!

00:21:57.640 --> 00:21:59.190
<i>Since I'll get the ura dora from the kan,</i>

00:21:59.190 --> 00:22:01.460
<i>winning off Achiga or drawing it 
myself will put me in first place.</i>

00:22:01.810 --> 00:22:04.340
<i>Ending in second place is just too lame!</i>

00:22:05.470 --> 00:22:06.720
<i>So you made your move, Oohoshi!</i>

00:22:07.240 --> 00:22:09.590
<i>But I'm in third place as the last dealer...</i>

00:22:09.590 --> 00:22:11.160
<i>Even if I have to break my tenpai,</i>

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:13.350
<i>I won't pull out now!</i>

00:22:13.950 --> 00:22:16.650
<i>That's actually it, you know?</i>

00:22:16.650 --> 00:22:20.520
<i>However, if I win off that, 
it'll only be a sanbaiman,</i>

00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:22.690
<i>and I'll be tied with Achiga.</i>

00:22:23.590 --> 00:22:26.250
<i>Achiga will be first because
 of dealer order precedence,</i>

00:22:26.250 --> 00:22:27.520
<i>and I'll be second.</i>

00:22:28.430 --> 00:22:30.370
<i>I will never allow that!</i>

00:22:32.740 --> 00:22:33.540
Chi.

00:22:34.780 --> 00:22:35.620
<i>Tenpai!</i>

00:22:37.360 --> 00:22:39.060
<i>The ippatsu is gone,</i>

00:22:39.720 --> 00:22:41.090
<i>but I'll still...</i>

00:22:45.190 --> 00:22:46.260
<i>...win!</i>

00:22:50.810 --> 00:22:51.800
Tsumo.

00:22:55.040 --> 00:22:55.910
6,000—

00:22:55.560 --> 00:22:56.510
Oohoshi-san.

00:22:57.530 --> 00:23:00.150
You should check for ura dora from the kan.

00:23:02.120 --> 00:23:04.650
Right. I guess that's the rule.

00:23:04.650 --> 00:23:07.130
<i>You still can't accept your defeat?</i>

00:23:07.130 --> 00:23:08.780
<i>How pathetic.</i>

00:23:12.600 --> 00:23:14.620
I'm sorry, Oohoshi-san.

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:16.830
That's no longer...

00:23:17.700 --> 00:23:19.550
your territory.

00:23:21.900 --> 00:23:24.450
The game is over!

00:23:24.450 --> 00:23:28.010
The first match of the 
semifinals is hereby complete!

00:23:24.900 --> 00:23:26.010
But...

00:23:28.220 --> 00:23:34.260
In first place is the dark horse 
Achiga Girls' Academy's Takakamo Shizuno!

00:23:34.820 --> 00:23:36.360
Thank you!

00:23:52.500 --> 00:23:53.530
Haru-chan...

00:23:56.400 --> 00:23:57.430
Haru-chan.

00:23:57.930 --> 00:23:58.770
Yeah...

00:23:59.180 --> 00:24:01.620
<i>The wall that I wasn't able 
to overcome in my time...</i>

00:24:02.590 --> 00:24:06.860
Since I belong to the group of 
people who suffered defeat here,

00:24:06.860 --> 00:24:10.220
I was afraid that I would not be able

00:24:10.220 --> 00:24:12.340
to honestly be happy if we won.

00:24:15.600 --> 00:24:16.850
But right now,

00:24:18.060 --> 00:24:19.590
all I feel is happiness.

00:24:20.240 --> 00:24:21.810
Even more than I could 
have felt for myself!

00:24:24.550 --> 00:24:26.820
Congratulations, everybody.

00:24:27.750 --> 00:24:28.950
Thank you.

00:24:31.730 --> 00:24:32.790
Haramura-san!

00:24:34.280 --> 00:24:38.940
Haramura-san went back while you 
were doing the hero interview.

00:24:38.940 --> 00:24:40.120
Oh man!

00:24:40.120 --> 00:24:43.510
She asked me to send 
you her humble regards.

00:24:43.510 --> 00:24:46.750
Oh, and she seemed to 
be enjoying herself.

00:24:46.750 --> 00:24:48.490
<b>Shindouji Girls'</b>

00:24:47.740 --> 00:24:50.470
Do you want some of these?

00:24:50.800 --> 00:24:51.760
What is that?

00:24:52.380 --> 00:24:56.510
A gift from one of my old 
middle school friends. Tacos.

00:24:56.790 --> 00:24:57.810
Tacos?

00:24:57.810 --> 00:24:59.310
Why those?

00:25:02.360 --> 00:25:03.650
Thank you.

00:25:04.890 --> 00:25:06.520
U-Um...

00:25:07.860 --> 00:25:09.910
I don't know what to say...

00:25:18.890 --> 00:25:20.330
<i>I'm so sad.</i>

00:25:20.850 --> 00:25:22.540
<i>I want to go to Ryuuka.</i>

00:25:23.300 --> 00:25:27.460
<i>I wonder if it would rain 
on her thighs right now.</i>

00:25:30.070 --> 00:25:33.170
I'm sorry, Teru!
 I came in second...

00:25:34.580 --> 00:25:37.180
We made it through the semifinals, 
so just win the next time.

00:25:37.780 --> 00:25:40.930
I'm going to fix my bad habits 
in two days and turn the tables.

00:25:41.240 --> 00:25:43.270
Me too! Next time, I...

00:25:44.450 --> 00:25:48.980
<i>The day after tomorrow, I'll beat 
you 100 times, Takakamo Shizuno!</i>

00:25:52.130 --> 00:25:54.190
It's warm from your body, Ako!

00:25:54.190 --> 00:25:55.820
What are you talking about?

00:25:55.820 --> 00:25:56.950
Did you say "warm"?

00:25:56.950 --> 00:26:03.190
Oh yeah, the finals will be held on 
yet another new, specially built stage.

00:26:04.070 --> 00:26:08.200
Only teams that made it to the finals 
are allowed to go look at it.

00:26:08.200 --> 00:26:10.710
So, please take me there,

00:26:11.260 --> 00:26:12.430
Captain.

00:26:15.090 --> 00:26:16.420
In your current condition,

00:26:16.420 --> 00:26:19.110
maybe you could even beat 
Kuro's dora domination.

00:26:20.440 --> 00:26:21.970
I think it's here.

00:26:23.830 --> 00:26:28.350
Apparently the soundproofing and radio 
shielding is better than the other stage.

00:26:28.350 --> 00:26:31.110
The glass has been 
replaced with walls, too.

00:26:31.520 --> 00:26:33.110
I hope it's warm.

00:26:34.340 --> 00:26:36.110
Let's go, Haru-chan.

00:26:54.640 --> 00:26:55.880
Akado-san...

00:26:56.410 --> 00:26:57.760
Pro player Kokaji...

00:26:59.710 --> 00:27:00.980
Long time no see.

00:27:01.400 --> 00:27:02.600
It's been a while.

00:27:03.290 --> 00:27:04.910
How come you're here today?

00:27:05.430 --> 00:27:08.350
<i>Huh, I'm not as scared 
as I thought I would be.</i>

00:27:08.780 --> 00:27:12.710
They got me a room in a hotel 
nearby until the finals,

00:27:12.710 --> 00:27:16.030
but when I'm not at home in 
my tracksuit, I just can't relax.

00:27:16.030 --> 00:27:18.110
So, I thought I'd take a walk to cool down.

00:27:18.590 --> 00:27:20.320
She's just like Shizu.

00:27:19.170 --> 00:27:21.710
I came here with my students to see the...

00:27:20.320 --> 00:27:21.710
How surprising.

00:27:23.840 --> 00:27:24.740
<i>Oh, I get it.</i>

00:27:25.380 --> 00:27:29.100
<i>These girls behind me are my confidence.</i>

00:27:30.440 --> 00:27:31.640
By the way,

00:27:33.280 --> 00:27:35.750
I decided to try my hand at 
being a pro player as well.

00:27:38.340 --> 00:27:41.310
Once I've watched them win, of course.

00:27:54.310 --> 00:27:55.980
All right, let's head back.

00:27:55.980 --> 00:27:56.740
Okay.

00:27:57.570 --> 00:27:59.600
I'm starving.

00:28:01.980 --> 00:28:02.870
Shizu?

00:28:11.810 --> 00:28:12.840
<i>Nodoka.</i>

00:28:15.320 --> 00:28:17.880
<i>Let's play here the day after tomorrow!</i>

00:28:27.410 --> 00:28:28.940
<i>Like we used to!</i>

00:28:42.790 --> 00:28:44.580
Let's go.

00:28:53.510 --> 00:28:56.170
Okay, let's move out!

00:28:58.830 --> 00:29:00.270
Let's crush them!

00:29:00.270 --> 00:29:02.260
I'll show 'em!

00:29:11.560 --> 00:29:13.220
<i>Nodoka, you're too slow!</i>

00:29:14.400 --> 00:29:16.770
<i>I bet you don't usually work out.</i>

00:29:19.380 --> 00:29:21.260
<i>I'm on my way.</i>

00:29:23.800 --> 00:29:25.820
In the 21st century,

00:29:25.820 --> 00:29:29.450
the number of mahjong players around
the world is in the hundreds of millions,

00:29:29.450 --> 00:29:33.540
and the professional players 
have an avid following.

00:29:34.210 --> 00:29:37.280
Even at the high school level, 
a large-scale national tournament

00:29:37.280 --> 00:29:38.790
is held every year.

00:29:38.790 --> 00:29:43.260
That's where the high 
school players compete

00:29:43.260 --> 00:29:46.910
in order to make it into the 
league of professionals.

00:29:47.470 --> 00:29:52.510
This is the path of the girls 
who were aiming for the top.
